{%- doc -%}
  Full-media overlay link for a hero slide (bmp_slide_link).

  Rendered as a direct child of <slideshow-slide>, BEFORE .slide__content:
  same z-index layer (--layer-flat), earlier sibling — so the content stack
  paints above it and its interactive elements win clicks (companion
  pointer-events rules in assets/bmp-styles.css). Accessible name: the slide
  image's alt, else the bmp.accessibility.bmp_slide_link_fallback string.

  DELIBERATE INVERSION of core's overlay-link idiom, which Horizon ships five
  times (blocks/_card.liquid:26, snippets/product-card.liquid:87,
  snippets/collection-card.liquid:64, snippets/resource-card.liquid:60,
  blocks/_featured-blog-posts-card.liquid:85). Core puts the overlay at
  --layer-raised (2), ABOVE the content, and relies on a pointer-events opt-in
  for descendants. A hero slide's content wrapper spans the whole slide, so the
  same arrangement made the link swallow taps over in-slide buttons under
  below-media grids. Do NOT "align with core" — the inversion IS the fix.

  @param {string} url - destination URL (block_settings.bmp_slide_link)
  @param {object} [image] - the slide's preview image (names the link)
{%- enddoc -%}
<a class="bmp-slide-link" href="{{ url }}">
  <span class="visually-hidden">
    {%- if image.alt != blank -%}
      {{- image.alt | escape -}}
    {%- else -%}
      {{- 'bmp.accessibility.bmp_slide_link_fallback' | t -}}
    {%- endif -%}
  </span>
</a>
